# Behavior-compare FAIL regression baseline.
#
# The CI `behavior-gate` job compares the observed FAIL count in
# behavior-report.md against the value on the LAST line of this file.
# The gate fails the build only on regression: observed FAIL > baseline.
#
# Baseline established 2026-09-13 (plan S2, docs/plans/2026-09-11-001 rev8):
#   - Environment: fresh dual-stack containers (o2oa/o2server v9.5.2 + postgres),
#     BOTH sides fully seeded — Java via scripts/seed_java.py --init --process-form
#     (org domain + testadmin + process application/flow + CMS app/form from
#     migration 091), Rust via auto-migrations + seed_fixtures.sql.
#   - Observed: 157 FAIL / 1856 PASS / 2029 SKIP (N1), 158/1855/2029 (N2)
#     across two fresh-environment runs → baseline 170 = observed + ~8%
#     environment headroom. Regressions pushing FAILs beyond 170 fail the gate.
#   - Session-destructive endpoints (logout/switchuser family) are skipped by
#     the comparator (is_session_destructive_endpoint) — executing one kills
#     the comparison session and poisons ~2000 subsequent requests.
#   - Remaining FAIL classes are the W12 convergence backlog (envelope/field
#     naming layer), see docs/audits/behavior-diff-clusters-2026-09-13.md.
170

